  "constructionChange": "Closed retained-fascicle packets supply dark optical mass on the existing connected shoots. Fine exterior needles decrease from80 to48 per shoot; two broad boughs bridge the right crown and the foreground crown is wider/higher. No crown envelope, alpha card, leaf sphere, hedge ball or camera-facing geometry.",
  "geometricReview": {
    "improved": [
      "Actual front and three-quarter views show substantially opaque layered crown pads, with most r04 inner twig lace concealed.",
      "Two bridging right boughs carry foliage across the former broad V gap while retaining supported layered branches.",
      "The foreground crown is wider and taller, with the same hidden root/base curve."
    ],
    "remaining": [
      "Close view still reveals repeated radial tuft patterns and some broad retained-rib grain; exact Japanese pine needle character remains unaccepted.",
      "The whole foreground standalone model includes its long concealed lower curve. Native roof occlusion must be checked after root integration.",
      "Standalone Cycles PBR and studio lighting do not prove native WebGL warm rim lighting or source-photo fidelity."
    ]
  },
